# Clear board menu action

Add a destructive Clear board action to the Board burger menu while preserving the current game setup and saved plans.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The Board burger menu contains `Clear board`.
- [x] Selecting it presents `This will remove all placed items and empty all hands. Are you sure?` with No and Yes actions.
- [x] No dismisses without changing game state.
- [x] Yes removes every road, settlement, and city.
- [x] Yes clears all players' resource and Victory Point cards, Largest Army, and Longest Road.
- [x] Terrain, number tokens, active players, orientation, and plans remain unchanged.
- [x] Cleared state persists through the normal active-game persistence boundary.
- [x] Domain and UI regression coverage compiles.

## Evidence

- Added `BoardState.clearPlacedItemsAndHands()` as the single domain mutation boundary.
- Added the destructive burger-menu action and confirmation alert to `BoardScreen`.
- Added domain coverage for cleared and preserved state plus a UI confirmation regression test.
- `xcodebuild build-for-testing -project HexIQ.xcodeproj -scheme HexIQ -destination 'generic/platform=iOS Simulator' CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO` compiled the changed app and test sources; Xcode subsequently stalled while finalising test products and was interrupted.

## Manual checks

- Confirm the menu wording, No/Yes behavior, and persisted cleared state on a simulator or device.
